<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
Privacy manifest for Verbinal on iPhone and iPad (plan 47 0.1). The Mac app has its own,
Verbinal/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy; this folder is left out of the Mac target and bundled at the root
of the iOS app, where App Store Connect looks for it.

Contents verified against the code compiled into VerbinalIOS (its SwiftFileList), 2026-10-22.

Required-reason APIs used:

  NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults
    Sources: settings and stores across the app (@AppStorage, UserDefaults.standard)
    Reason:
      CA92.1 — access info from the same app

  NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp
    Sources:
      Storage/Services/VOSpaceBrowserService.swift   — fileSizeKey / .size of a file to upload
      Storage/ViewModels/StorageBrowserModel.swift   — the same, before an upload
      VerbinalKit Networking/NetworkClient.swift     — fileSizeKey / .size of a file to upload
      VerbinalKit Storage/AppSupport.swift           — contentModificationDate of the app's own folders
      iOS/Open/Services/RemoteFileCache.swift        — size and date of files cached in Caches (least recent go first)
      iOS/Open/Models/FileRef.swift                  — the size of a file the person picked in Files
    Reasons:
      C617.1 — files inside the app's container (caches, downloads, stores)
      3B52.1 — files the person chose (document picker, "Open in Verbinal")

APIs NOT used (grep of the iOS file list, 2026-10-22):
  NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategorySystemBootTime  — no systemUptime / mach_absolute_time
  NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryDiskSpace       — no volumeAvailableCapacity / volumeTotalCapacity
  NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryActiveKeyboard  — no activeInputModes

Data collection: as the Mac app. The person's CADC username and password go to CADC, over TLS, to
sign in to their own account; linked to that identity, for the app's function, never for tracking.
No tracking, analytics or ad frameworks.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
    <false/>
    <key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
    <array/>

    <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
    <array>
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeUserID</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
            <true/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
            <false/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
            <array>
                <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
            </array>
        </dict>
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeCredentials</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
            <true/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
            <false/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
            <array>
                <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
            </array>
        </dict>
    </array>

    <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
    <array>
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
            <array>
                <string>CA92.1</string>
            </array>
        </dict>
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
            <array>
                <string>C617.1</string>
                <string>3B52.1</string>
            </array>
        </dict>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
